<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUSTCATHEDRAL_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 §3/§6. A DUPLICATE of
  src/RimUtinni/RustCathedralRoaches/Defs/ThingDefs_Races/RUT_CathedralRoach.xml,
  not a rename/move — the frozen twin's own line
  (src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Defs/BiomeDefs/RUT_RustCathedral.xml:103,
  after this item's freeze header lands) still needs the ORIGINAL
  RUT_CathedralRoach to keep working until Phase B, per the item's own §3
  "third option": ship RM_CathedralRoach here, leave RUT_CathedralRoach (and
  its own BodyDef/ThinkTree/mod, mandrake.rut.rustcathedralroaches)
  untouched in place as frozen-twin content. That donor mod is NOT absorbed
  by this build — only RustCathedralHum and RustCathedralWalls are (see this
  mod's About.xml). RUT_ScarRoach, the organic Scarlands sibling in that
  same donor mod, is likewise left alone (item §6: "open trade... do not
  silently absorb it" — hand-off, not decision, belongs to a Scarlands mod
  build).

  Renamed for this copy, tier-grammar-compliant since this is now genuinely
  new content living in a mandrake.rm.* mod: RUT_CathedralRoach ->
  RM_CathedralRoach (ThingDef+PawnKindDef), RUT_RoachHex -> RM_RoachHex
  (BodyDef — a second global defName RUT_RoachHex would collide with the
  original), RUT_CathedralRoachShell -> RM_CathedralRoachShell
  (butcherProducts), RUT_ThinkTree_CathedralRoach -> RM_ThinkTree_CathedralRoach
  (thinkTreeMain). texPath points at this mod's own copied art
  (Textures/Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_CathedralRoach/, byte-identical copies of
  the original's real, non-placeholder art). Everything else — stats, body
  layout, modExtension — is unchanged from the original; see that file's own
  header for the full donor/design rationale (LingLuo.Cockroach clone,
  bodySize/armor/healthScale reasoning).
-->
<Defs>

